## §9 — Condense
**Pattern (the wave's headline, §9 rule fired):** Amendment A13 — landed last cycle precisely to cure receipt incompleteness — met its first full wave, and **zero of five items cleared jev-prewave**. Every builder REPORTED its mechanical checks clean (harness assertions all PASS on all five final builds; A6 legs reported at 0 HITs on both legs for three items — T204 · T205 · T210 — with carried-with-disposition HITs on T199's fit leg and T208's census leg) — and three of those clean summaries were themselves found overstated by the re-fire returns (T204's fit row · T205's census rows · T205's CP01 PASS-at-0 ms against its failing 570 ms endpoint; §5 carries the itemized corrections) and every HOLD was ASSERTED-CHECKS on receipt grounds (the returns' own checking basis varies and is qualified in §9b.4 — T204/T210 are paperwork reviews; T205's re-fire independently evaluated its CP01 predicate and found the build failing the written strict bound, a stronger finding than a missing receipt): T199 (two index-line gaps in the fed paperwork, per its return's findings 1–2 and Limits: A-8's claimed probe inside the plate-owned window [0,800) has no filed dump in that window — the earliest filed dump is at 800 ms · B-17's swap receipt prints scale without the observed color the line claimed) · T204 (endpoint receipts + swap moved-instant receipts for five checkpoints + a fit row filed as a product instead of a measured bbox) · T205 (a strict-bound receipt failing at exactly 0.30 with no receipt at that instant · a fixed "8000ms" label in place of an evaluated instant · census rows overstating two phases' runtime effect) · T208 (timing-swap movement evidence for seven checkpoints via the inputs each assertion actually reads · a guard-#2 geometry receipt under content swap) · T210 (a hold-dependent swap probe · one stale index line printing a superseded value against its own receipt · CP9 without a whole-state equality receipt · palette swap without observed output values). The prewave own-checks dimension moved with cure rounds, stated by item (firing 1 → firing 2): T204 0.35→0.40 · T205 0.25→0.40 · T208 0.40→0.48 · T210 0.35→0.45 · T199 0.40→0.70 across cycles (Wave-33 firing 2 → this completion re-fire) — but never crossed. The defect is no longer enumeration (A13's index exists on every item and reconciliations were performed) — it is **receipt validity at the margin**: receipts that are present, plausible, and one predicate short of what their assertion prescribes, plus index lines whose claims outrun their receipts. On this wave's nine reviewed firings, the judges caught every one of these; the builders' self-reconciliation did not. WHY the self-reconciliation missed them is **not established by this wave's evidence** — shared authorship (the same author writes the claim and checks it) is one hypothesis consistent with the filings, priced as a hypothesis in the candidate below, not as the pattern's cause.

**Candidate amendment (filed, NOT landed — priced for HQ): RECEIPT-INDEPENDENCE.** The A13 reconciliation gains a second pair of eyes: before the prewave payload is assembled, the receipt index is reconciled by a checker that did not author the build record — in this seat's form, a mechanical cross-check script where the assertion is mechanical (every CONFIG-expression receipt re-evaluated by script and diffed against the filed value; every claimed probe instant grepped in the filed raw output) plus the seat's spot re-probe of the index's highest-risk lines (swap receipts + endpoint receipts — swap-related receipt defects are named in all five of this wave's final HOLD returns, T205's missing moved CP10/CP11 probes included). Evidence: 5 items, one wave, one defect class, against A13's own prediction (Cycle 036 §0b.1: the index "is priced to cut the re-fire count" — the observed result this wave: four first attempts each used a re-fire, T199 used its carried completion re-fire, and none cleared; with one wave and no clearance cohort, the size of any A13 effect on re-fire frequency remains unestablished). Landing form (instruction step · mechanical guard · Jev definition · Codex prompt) is HQ's pricing; this cycle files the candidate with its evidence and does not amend INSTRUCTION.md, because a second consecutive self-authored amendment to the same leg, landed the cycle after A13's first full wave produced zero clearances (its effect on re-fire frequency unestablished, its failure mode not yet causally priced), is exactly the calibration-instead-of-pricing pattern the judgment-layer evaluation exists to catch. NOT-YET-AMENDED, consumer HQ.

