27:- Dimensions (0–1): queue-state-priced · prior-scores-read · mechanics-seen · variables-extracted · guidance-carried · consumer-named. (1.0 = evidenced in the record with citations; 0.5 = asserted without citation; 0.0 = absent.)
28:- Rejection taxonomy (one primary per returned item): QUEUE-STALE (queue position/status not read this cycle) · REATTEMPT-MISROUTED (scored technique in a first-attempt wave) · SCORES-UNREAD (prior scores/cures exist, uncited) · MECHANICS-UNSEEN (no firsthand sub-beat record) · VARIABLES-THIN (variable list cannot bind a parameter table) · GUIDANCE-DROPPED (standing family guidance absent from working memory) · CONSUMER-VAGUE.
32:- Any dimension < 0.5 → RETURN-TO-OBSERVE for that item. GUIDANCE-DROPPED on a particle-field or typography item → RETURN-TO-OBSERVE at any other score (T15 attempt 1's founding lesson: the frozen-flow defect and both owner catches were guidance-shaped failures discovered only after the wave was spent).
