**REVISE — correct the mechanical guard coverage and record the T205 feed omission. The HQ deferral, score binding, and wave re-pricing pass.**

1. **Amendment faithfulness — ACCEPT.** RECEIPT-INDEPENDENCE is faithfully filed as NOT-YET-AMENDED. The closed HQ entry confirms the handoff, and `RUN.md` §9b.1 names the owning surfaces and three concrete acceptance cases: T199’s missing in-window probe, T199’s missing observed swap color, and T205’s failing endpoint predicate. `INSTRUCTION.md` §5 leg 3b still assigns reconciliation to the builder. The draft accurately leaves the cause of the misses and the proposed cure’s effectiveness open. [RUN.md §9b.1](RUN.md#L95) · [HQ.json, Wave 34](../../HQ.json#L404) · [INSTRUCTION.md §5](../../INSTRUCTION.md#L49)

2. **Four-layer coverage — REVISE.** The operative mechanical bullet misidentifies two commands. Command 3 covers syntax and determinism. Cite the five build records’ syntax and RNG receipts as builder-filed evidence. Command 5 covers segment binding. Cite each record’s cut window and `ffprobe` receipt, and distinguish those from the recreation HTML hashes recomputed in §5. Keep T205’s CP01 endpoint failure under the A11/A13 readiness and receipt-validation deferral. Keep T199’s A-8 assignment to command 8 unresolved pending evidence of a governing named zero-state anchor. The instruction, Jev, and Codex dispositions otherwise account for their untouched surfaces. [RUN.md §9 mechanical bullet](RUN.md#L89) · [guards.md, commands 3–8](../../guards/guards.md#L12) · [INSTRUCTION.md, A13](../../INSTRUCTION.md#L130)

3. **Feed completeness — REVISE.** T205’s first prewave return says command 8 was absent from the supplied excerpt and the reviewer retrieved it from disk. The prewave FED contract requires the guard command list. Record the omission in §9 disposition 4 and the §7 deviation register, with a named feeder disposition. The return independently identifies substantive HOLD grounds, so the omission leaves the HOLD standing. Also reconcile the duplication count: §9 says all nine prewave returns were duplicated, which with eight seat-gate returns already exceeds §7’s total of 13 before counting Condense. File a reconciled tally or mark the total unverified. [T205 first prewave return, Limits](../../../../study/recreations/T205-vote-to-grid-conversion-diagram/codex/jev-prewave.md#L1924) · [jev-prewave FED contract](../../guards/jev-prewave.md#L13) · [RUN.md §9 disposition 4](RUN.md#L83) · [RUN.md §7 deviation register](RUN.md#L128)

4. **Score-evidence binding — ACCEPT.** The filed prewave returns support the itemized own-checks deltas: T199 0.40→0.70 across cycles, T204 0.35→0.40, T205 0.25→0.40, T208 0.40→0.48, and T210 0.35→0.45. §9b.4 points to the returns, and verdict-history records five NO VERDICT rows with no lens scores. [RUN.md §9b.4](RUN.md#L98) · [verdict-history.md, Wave 34](../../verdict-history.md#L122)

5. **Wave re-pricing — ACCEPT.** Eight Phase A calls, eight exit-gate calls, and nine prewave calls yield 25 firings before Condense. With zero scored verdicts, firings per scored item is undefined. The draft keeps the Cycle 036 comparator unreconciled and carries wave size and cadence forward pending measured cost. [RUN.md §9 disposition 6](RUN.md#L85)

**Limits.** This review checked the filed records and governing text. It did not replay the builds or measure per-item wall time.

